WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.300
One shipment. Four parties. Four stories.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
A normal oracle crushes them into one answer.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.000
Concordance keeps the disagreement: what is settled, what is contested, and by how much.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.000
Five validators, five different models, each read every account on their own.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.600
They agree on a small, bounded record, the part that holds up on real validators.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.600
It also says why parties differ.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.600
Evidence can settle facts. No evidence settles meaning.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.400
When the dispute is about meaning, ask the clause one narrow question.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.800
Validators answer in one word. Consensus on one word is easy.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.600
The record updates. Ambiguity 38 → 18.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.200
Remove each party in turn.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:03.400
Before money moves, see which single voice the verdict hangs on.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.400
A second contract pays by the record.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.000
43% now. The rest after the ruling. No intermediary.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.800
The gate never changed. The oracle did.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.200
We measured it. The first design failed on real validators.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.800
So we redesigned it, and we say what is still open.

